x+ky \\\\ 2(ky)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}k(x+y) \\\\ k(2y)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =k[\\begin{aligned}x+y \\\\ 2y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 2({y}_{1}+{y}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{y}_{1} \\\\ 2{y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}+{y}_{2} \\\\ 2{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true." 13194139533948 true] [17592186268005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268006 13194139533948 true] [17592186268005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268007 13194139533948 true] [17592186268005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268008 13194139533948 true] [17592186268005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268009 13194139533948 true] [17592186268005 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268010 13194139533948 true] [17592186268005 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533948 true] [17592186268005 1041 "selection" 13194139533948 true] [17592186268005 1104 #edb/ref 17592186268006 13194139533948 true] [17592186268005 1110 #uuid "48d49dd3-04d8-5449-9d2a-f2ea6067e69d" 13194139533948 true] [17592186268006 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139533948 true] [17592186268006 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533948 true] [17592186268006 1111 #uuid "6a2275b7-0cd4-5acd-ad72-a48b0b2500ef" 13194139533948 true] [17592186268007 1034 "I only" 13194139533948 true] [17592186268007 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533948 true] [17592186268007 1111 #uuid "c277f7b3-76e0-5e40-b67a-d1147b5db584" 13194139533948 true] [17592186268008 1034 "III only" 13194139533948 true] [17592186268008 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533948 true] [17592186268008 111